id: pm-beads-1uz3
title: Canonicalize complete workspace reads and adopt the current pm host contract
description: "pm-beads still invokes deprecated list-all with legacy full/include-body aliases, accepts some unverifiable completeness receipts, keeps ignored manifest.pm metadata, exact-pins development to pm 2026.8.15, and leaves most pm-changelog reads bounded or host-ambiguous. Migrate the import/export reference to the current canonical CLI/SDK contract without conflating independent privacy or full-coverage blockers."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[5]: agent-ux,compatibility,completeness,latest-cli,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-21T05:20:59.581Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T05:46:27.942Z"
assignee: codex
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: Create red-first tests for exact canonical pm list --all argv with output-include full plus unbounded output budget and limit; fail closed on absent or malformed completeness omission count total row identity and duplicate receipts; remove only ignored manifest metadata and validate the complete raw manifest through the public SDK at the minimum and current development hosts; exact-pin development to pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.21 while retaining a justified minimum behavior floor; route every package and release-workflow changelog read through the project CLI with both output bounds disabled; update dependencies to latest compatible published versions; run the full repository release gate and report its literal non-100 coverage dimensions; prove packed npm and Bun behavior on separate real trackers with empty alias-deprecation stderr; link CI PR and exact-head reviewer outcomes; do not merge or publish while pm-beads-lajb or pm-beads-cjey remains open
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: pm-beads main d4f36b5; installed and npm-latest pm CLI/SDK 2026.8.21; npm pm-beads 2026.8.16
repro_steps: Run the real workspace read and inspect child stderr for list-all deprecation; inspect readPmItems argv and receipt decoder; pass complete manifest.json to the public 2026.8.21 SDK; inspect package and workflow changelog invocations.
expected_result: pm-beads uses canonical deprecation-free complete reads and current SDK contracts while failing closed on unverifiable corpus evidence and preserving independent release blockers.
actual_result: "Baseline release check passes 115 tests with 50 documented declarations and zero production vulnerabilities, but coverage is only 93.40/80.33/95.28 lines/branches/functions over index.ts; the current raw manifest has an ignored pm key under SDK 2026.8.21."
component: Beads workspace integration and release plumbing
customer_impact: Import and export agents depend on a complete tracker corpus; deprecated or unverifiable reads can silently omit work or pollute machine-readable stderr.
